From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Orchard migration <noreply@orchardlinux>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:32:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] iommu: apple-dart: Don't dereference a master config in
 the S5L8960X fault handler

apple_dart_s5l8960x_irq() looks up dev_iommu_priv_get(dart->dev) to add
the master's DMA window base to the reported fault address. dart->dev is
the DART itself, which is not behind an IOMMU, so the lookup returns NULL
and every translation fault oopses in interrupt context.

A fault cannot be attributed to one master's window here anyway, so
report the address register as read.

Fixes: S5L8960X DART support from the Hoolock 090-dart series.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index 01737458b..f7eee85ea 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -1292,7 +1292,6 @@ static const struct iommu_ops apple_dart_iommu_ops = {
 static irqreturn_t apple_dart_s5l8960x_irq(int irq, void *dev)
 {
 	struct apple_dart *dart = dev;
-	struct apple_dart_master_cfg *cfg = dev_iommu_priv_get(dart->dev);
 	const char *fault_name = NULL;
 	u32 error = readl(dart->regs + DART_S5L8960X_ERROR);
 	u32 error_code = FIELD_GET(DART_S5L8960X_ERROR_CODE, error);
@@ -1318,8 +1317,8 @@ static irqreturn_t apple_dart_s5l8960x_irq(int irq, void *dev)
 
 	dev_err_ratelimited(
 		dart->dev,
-		"translation fault: status:0x%x stream:%d code:0x%x (%s) at 0x%llx",
-		error, stream_idx, error_code, fault_name, addr | cfg->dma_min);
+		"translation fault: status:0x%x stream:%d code:0x%x (%s) at 0x%x",
+		error, stream_idx, error_code, fault_name, addr);
 
 	writel(error, dart->regs + DART_S5L8960X_ERROR);
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
